{"id":"hanani","name":"Hanani","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:hanani"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hanani","text":"God has gratified me, or is gracious. (1.) One of the sons of Heman (1 Chr. 25:4, 25). (2.) A prophet who was sent to rebuke king Asa for entering into a league with Benhadad I., king of Syria, against Judah (2 Chr. 16:1-10). He was probably the father of the prophet Jehu (1 Kings 16:7). (3.) Probably a brother of Nehemiah (Neh. 1:2; 7:2), who reported to him the melancholy condition of Jerusalem. Nehemiah afterwards appointed him to have charge of the city gates."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2607","lemma":"חֲנָנִי","xlit":"Chănânîy","gloss":"Chanani, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Hanani","count":11,"share":1},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":4,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":7,"share":0.64},{"strong":"H1697","lemma":"דָּבָר","xlit":"dâbâr","gloss":"a word","kjv":"act, advice, affair, answer","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":3,"share":0.27}],"verses":["1Kgs.16.1","1Kgs.16.7","1Chr.25.4","1Chr.25.25","2Chr.16.7","2Chr.19.2","2Chr.20.34","Ezra.10.20","Neh.1.2","Neh.7.2","Neh.12.36"],"related":[{"id":"jehu","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.044,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asahel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"azareel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"bethuel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"brother","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"commerce","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"cononiah",